Wi-Fi setup: enter the two-letter country code, for example GB. UK is accepted as GB; blank Enter keeps the current country. Enter the SSID exactly as configured, then the password. Password entry is hidden and Speakup key echo is temporarily off. Blank password is for an open network. Command letters and punctuation in SSID/password are literal. Ctrl+C cancels entry. After password entry: e returns to the fields for editing; q quits without changing the connection; Space connects using the entered details and saves the connection; h repeats this help. A connection may take up to two minutes. Connected confirms Wi-Fi, not internet access. At Country?, h then Enter opens this help.
